<title>GERMANY: Deutsche puts MGAM costs at 1.1-1.2 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>Deutsche puts MGAM costs at 1.1-1.2 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank Chief Executive Hilmar Kopper said on Wednesday the total cost of the problems at its British fund unit Morgan Grenfell Asset Management (MGAM) amounted to a some 1.1 to 1.2 billion marks ($712.2 million).</p>
<p>&quot;We don't know yet exactly, the calculations are still continuing,&quot; Kopper told a news conference. ($ = 1.685 German Marks)</p>
</text>
